ared gas-phase static VASP input directory (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR).\", \"source\": \"task_01\"}], \"final_status\": \"done\", \"task_count\": 0, \"completed_task_count\": 0}\n\nEditable file snapshot (authoritative):\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/MEMORY.md\">\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Completed O2 gas-phase input preparation from `structures/o2/o2.vasp` (task_01).\n- Current milestone: Relax + static prepare steps succeeded with required tool-level `user_incar_settings` and verified INCAR/KPOINTS content.\n- Latest run artifact: `vasp_inputs/o2_relax_user/o2`, `vasp_inputs/o2_static_user/o2`.\n- Next action: Ready for downstream VASP execution/analysis if requested.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. INCAR overrides must be passed directly via prepare-tool `user_incar_settings` (no post-generation patching).\n2. If direct `user_incar_settings` passing is unavailable, task must be reported as blocked (no workaround).\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. None.\n\n## Pointers\n- Goal / principles: MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\">\n# GOAL\n\n## TL;DR\n- Primary objective: Prepare gas-phase VASP relax and static input sets for O2 using the existing seed structure `structures/o2/o2.vasp`.\n- Definition of success: both prepare tools succeed, required INCAR overrides are present, and KPOINTS is Gamma-centered `1 1 1` for both setups.\n- Non-goals: running VASP jobs, post-generation INCAR editing, or changing the seed structure geometry/composition.\n\n## Objectives\n- Generate relax inputs via `vasp_relax_prepare` (`calc_type='gas'`) into `vasp_inputs/o2_relax_user`.\n- Generate static inputs via `vasp_sp_prepare` (`calc_type='gas'`) into `vasp_inputs/o2_static_user`.\n- Enforce spin/magnetization and convergence overrides through tool-native `user_incar_settings`.\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Relax directory created successfully with INCAR containing: `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM` from `{\"O\":1}` (expanded to two O atoms), `EDIFFG=-0.015`.\n- Static directory created successfully with INCAR containing: `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM` from `{\"O\":1}`, `NSW=0`, `IBRION=-1`, `EDIFF=1e-7`.\n- Both KPOINTS files are Gamma-centered `1 1 1`.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No electronic/ionic execution results (energies, forces, frequencies) are produced in this task.\n- No manual/bash/python patching of generated INCAR files.\n\n## Change log\n- [2026-03-01] Goal clarified and completed for O2 gas-phase relax/static input preparation with direct `user_incar_settings` enforcement and INCAR/KPOINTS verification.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\">\n# FACTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Canonical definitions: O2 gas-phase prepare templates and required spin-polarized overrides are now instantiated for relax and static workflows.\n- Verified facts: both generated input sets contain requested INCAR overrides and Gamma `1 1 1` KPOINTS.\n- Tentative hypotheses: (empty)\n\n## Canonical Definitions\n- For this O2 setup, `MAGMOM: {\"O\": 1}` expands to `MAGMOM = 2*1.0` (µB per atom initialization for the 2-atom cell).\n\n## Verified Facts\n- Relax preparation succeeded at `vasp_inputs/o2_relax_user/o2` using tool-level overrides; INCAR contains `ISPIN = 2`, `NUPDOWN = 2.0`, `MAGMOM = 2*1.0`, `EDIFFG = -0.015` (force convergence mode, eV/Å).  \n  Evidence: `vasp_inputs/o2_relax_user/o2/INCAR` (task_01).\n- Static preparation succeeded at `vasp_inputs/o2_static_user/o2` using tool-level overrides; INCAR contains `ISPIN = 2`, `NUPDOWN = 2.0`, `MAGMOM = 2*1.0`, `NSW = 0`, `IBRION = -1`, `EDIFF = 1e-07` (electronic convergence, eV).  \n  Evidence: `vasp_inputs/o2_static_user/o2/INCAR` (task_01).\n- Both generated KPOINTS files are Gamma-centered single-point meshes (`Gamma` then `1 1 1`).  \n  Evidence: `vasp_inputs/o2_relax_user/o2/KPOINTS`, `vasp_inputs/o2_static_user/o2/KPOINTS` (task_01).\n\n## Tentative\n- (empty)\n\n## Decision Log\n- [task_01] Used prepare-tool-native `user_incar_settings` exactly as specified for both relax and static generation.\n  - Rationale: hard constraint forbids any post-generation INCAR patching.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\">\n# FILES\n\n## TL;DR\n- Entry points: `structures/o2/o2.vasp`.\n- Primary artifacts: prepared gas-phase relax/static VASP input directories for O2.\n\n## Index\n- PATH: structures/o2/o2.vasp | kind=structure | desc=Seed O2 structure used as input for relax/static preparation. | source=task_01\n- PATH: vasp_inputs/o2_relax_user/o2 | kind=dir | desc=Prepared gas-phase relaxation VASP input directory (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR). | source=task_01\n- PATH: vasp_inputs/o2_static_user/o2 | kind=dir | desc=Prepared gas-phase static VASP input directory (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR). | source=task_01\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\">\n# CONSTRAINTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Hard constraints:\n  - INCAR overrides must be passed directly through prepare-tool `user_incar_settings`.\n  - No INCAR patching via bash/python after generation.\n  - If direct `user_incar_settings` passing is unavailable, report blocked (no workaround).\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Use `calc_type='gas'` for both relax and static preparation of this O2 case. (task_01 packet)\n- Do not modify INCAR via shell/python patching; only tool-native arguments are allowed. (task_01 packet)\n- If required `user_incar_settings` cannot be passed directly to prepare tools, terminate as blocked with exact reason. (task_01 packet)\n\n## Soft Preferences\n- Verify completion by checking key INCAR tags and confirming KPOINTS is Gamma-centered `1 1 1`.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\">\n# QUESTIONS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Active blockers: none.\n\n## Active\n- (empty)\n\n## Resolved\n- Q: Can all required INCAR overrides be applied directly via prepare-tool `user_incar_settings` (without manual patching)?\n  - A: Yes, for both relax and static preparations.\n  - Evidence: `vasp_inputs/o2_relax_user/o2/INCAR` and `vasp_inputs/o2_static_user/o2/INCAR` contain requested tags (task_01).\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\">\n# RUNBOOK\n\n## TL;DR\n- Standard operating procedure pointer file.\n\n## Checklist\n1. Confirm goal and success criteria from task packet.\n2. Read MEMORY.md first, then locate details via rg/sed.\n3. Persist large outputs to files and cite paths.\n4. Finish by returning one structured TaskOutput response.\n\n</editable_file>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": null, "__class__": "HumanMessage", "__type__": "human"}
